      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945962/assets/31e0e843eb581f01cdc7ebb5273398a3c0f32d2949b9e36cd28423295d7b76e8.png)\n\nThe speed-time graph shown above represents the motion of a $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle. At what times is the motorcycle accelerating?",
      "worked_solution": "The motorcycle is accelerating when its acceleration is positive. In a speed-time graph, the acceleration is given by the slope of the line. So, we need to find the times for which the slope is positive.\n\nWe see from the graph that the slope is positive from $t=30\\,\\text{s}$ to $t=60\\,\\text{s}.$ Therefore, the $250\\text{cc}$ motorcycle is accelerating in this time interval.",
